        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andrei Platonov, Andrei Platonovich Klimentov, John Edward Masefield\n- Works: The Foundation Pit, The Midnight Folk\n- Roles: Soviet Russian writer, playwright, poet, Poet Laureate of the United Kingdom\n- Concepts: existentialism\n\nFacts:\n- John Edward Masefield was born on 1 June 1878 and died on 12 May 1967.\n- Andrei Platonovich Klimentov was born on 28 August 1899 and died on 5 January 1951.\n- Andrei Platonovich Klimentov used the pen name Andrei Platonov.\n- John Edward Masefield was an English poet and writer.\n- Andrei Platonov was a Soviet Russian writer, playwright, and poet whose works anticipate existentialism.\n- The Midnight Folk is a children's fantasy novel by John Masefield that was first published in 1927.\n- John Masefield became Poet Laureate of the United Kingdom in 1930.\n- The Foundation Pit is a gloomy, symbolic, and semi-satirical novel by Andrei Platonov.",
